{
  "abstract": "We study the anchored order-five source that supplies sixteen of the twenty-one square conditions for a rational Diophantine septuple. For a rational five-cycle with individual adjacent roots, five linear equations in three coefficients recognize membership in the source. We prove that a consistent fit with positive radical closure forces the order-five parameter relation, including exclusion of singular rational exceptions. Separate square conditions retain the anchor and matching lifts. The normalization of the full matching surface is an abelian surface obtained from two elliptic curves by a diagonal translation of order two; its shared matching twists are translation torsors rather than ordinary quadratic twists. A signed translation of order four swaps the anchors and preserves the ordered physical tails. At an inhabited rational parameter, certified descent determines the surface group as $\\mathbb Z^3\\oplus C_{20}\\oplus C_2$ and shows that every physical tuple has an untwisted representative. Uniform non-isogeny and explicit pole calculations exclude rational or elliptic curves over $\\mathbb Q$ in the sufficient completion divisor at every admissible fixed rational parameter. Over the minimal product-lift function field, complementary complete two-descent images at two rank-one specializations prove that the anchor cover and base have rank zero and only boundary points. An explicit quadratic extension attains the smallest possible extension degree and carries all sixteen roots on a genus-four base. Exact symbolic certificates, saved certified arithmetic, and a standalone rational recognizer accompany the proofs. No rational septuple or classification of the remaining completion points is claimed.",
